From: gt510 <gt510@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] software_isp: debayer co-sited Bayer cells from one filtered texel

The SR544 (SM-T550 rear camera) binned modes (1296x972, 1280x720) emit
Bayer frames whose four 2x2-cell samples were taken at one spot: the raw
planes are offset by ~0 instead of the Bayer half-cell, measured on raw
frames (B/Gb/Gr/R plane cross-correlation). Standard demosaicing then
places red ~1 px down-right and blue ~1 px up-left of green: purple and
yellow fringes on every sharp edge.

With software_isp: cosited_max_width set, RAW10 CSI-2 inputs up to that
width are unpacked on the CPU into one (R, G, B, G) RGBA texel per cell and
the GPU debayer becomes a single bilinear texture lookup per pixel (was
nine packed-byte fetches), which also makes it much cheaper.
---
diff --git a/src/libcamera/shaders/bayer_1x_packed.frag b/src/libcamera/shaders/bayer_1x_packed.frag
index e2d8753..9563eaf 100644
--- a/src/libcamera/shaders/bayer_1x_packed.frag
+++ b/src/libcamera/shaders/bayer_1x_packed.frag
@@ -104,6 +104,14 @@ void main(void)
 {
 	vec3 rgb;
 
+#if defined (COSITED)
+	/*
+	 * The texture holds one (R, G, B, G) texel per co-sited 2x2 Bayer
+	 * cell; its bilinear filter does the interpolation.
+	 */
+	vec4 cell = texture2D(tex_y, textureOut);
+	rgb = vec3(cell.r, (cell.g + cell.a) * 0.5, cell.b);
+#else
 	/*
 	 * center_bytes holds the coordinates of the MS byte of the pixel
 	 * being sampled on the [0, stride-1/height-1] range.
@@ -271,6 +279,8 @@ void main(void)
 			vec3(patterns.y, C, patterns.x) :
 			vec3(patterns.wz, C));
 
+#endif
+
 	/*
 	 * \todo: Black level normalising, AWB and digital gain could be
 	 * reworked into a single multiplication.
